# Day 37

## Experiment Title

Understanding Maven Build Lifecycle


## Objective

To study the different phases of the Maven build lifecycle and understand their purpose in application development.


## Theory

The Maven build lifecycle consists of a sequence of phases used to build and manage applications systematically. Common phases include validate, compile, test, package, install, and deploy.

Each phase performs a specific task in the software development process. Maven executes these phases automatically in the correct order, which simplifies application development and reduces manual work.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Maven project directory.

Study the different phases of the Maven build lifecycle.

Execute Maven lifecycle commands for the project.

Observe the sequence of operations performed during execution.

Verify the generated build files and installation process.


## Output

The Maven build lifecycle phases were executed successfully.

Application compilation, testing, and packaging processes completed properly.

Build files and project artifacts were generated successfully.


## Result

Successfully understood the Maven build lifecycle and its phases in application development.
